-- l4 batch over an export whose own input's default SUPPLIES a section input
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W7). The default reads nothing of `base`, so
-- `base` is no input of the export: binding it to the row would make the `WITH`
-- in the default a WITH to a bound input, which is not a supply, and every row
-- would be refused.

§ `Supplied`
    GIVEN base IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 4

GIVETH A NUMBER
`double it` MEANS base TIMES 2

@export default Scaled
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (`double it` WITH base IS 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES 100
